model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway.poolMembership {
    metadata {
      constraint "The hourly pool migration inventory also reports the pool ownership population, read-only, in its own transaction and snapshot, after its own reads and in a savepoint of their transaction, so a report statement that fails or is cancelled leaves the inventory's reads, outcome and lines exactly as they were. The population is every pair a pool token can name: each record in an organization's basaltPools, each recorded app with the organization that owns it, and each copy of the basalt-pool package with its owner. Each pair is classified by the ownership check's own exported rule, never a second copy of it. The report writes one line after the inventory's own, pool-ownership-v1, with counts by shape, the number of organizations whose metadata is not JSON, and at most 50 pool ids of pairs that would be refused, never organization metadata. It reads at most 1,001 pairs under the inventory's 3 s statement limit, and it writes the line with complete false and a reason, row_cap, query_failed or inventory_failed, whenever it could not cover every pair. It changes no answer and writes nothing."
    }
  }
}
